# No SPA-fallback 200-rewrite block here on purpose. A prior version of
# this file had rules like "/guides/* / 200" intended to fall back to the
# SPA shell for paths not covered by prerendering yet - but Cloudflare
# Pages applies _redirects rules BEFORE checking whether a matching static
# asset already exists, so every one of those wildcard rules was silently
# hijacking its own already-prerendered pages (e.g. /guides/bearded-dragon/,
# /encyclopedia/category/small-mammals/) and serving the fully-baked
# homepage's HTML in their place - confirmed live via curl showing the
# homepage's <title> and canonical on dozens of unrelated pages, caught by
# an Ahrefs crawl. This broke canonical/title/og-tags sitewide.
#
# Static assets are always served correctly with no rule needed here at
# all - every guide/encyclopedia/blog/static page (plus /pack, noindex but
# prerendered anyway for a stable default-state file - see prerender.mjs)
# is prerendered, so Cloudflare finds and serves the real file directly.
# For the couple of routes with no stable default to prerender (e.g.
# /donate/success, /donate/cancel depend on Stripe redirect query params),
# Cloudflare's automatic 404.html handling serves a real 404 status - but
# since this is a client-side-routed SPA, React Router reads the actual
# browser URL on mount regardless of which HTML/status was initially
# served, so a real visitor's JS still loads and renders the correct page
# either way. Only a non-JS crawler hitting one of those exact couple of
# noindex routes would see a 404 instead of a soft 200 - an acceptable
# trade for not breaking SEO tags on every real, indexed page on the site.

